> Note that barbarians max out as Basic in both dagger and box.
> I think multifire starts at Skilled so barbarians single fire
> any missile.  At single fire, either damage per shot (light
> missiles) or damage per weight in a single shot (comparing
> maybe daggers to spears) dominates.  IIRC spears do stack but
> they never multifire so even though a barbarian can get to
> skilled in spear it's not usually worth carrying a heavy stack
> of them.

On the other hand, spears do more damage than either arrows or
daggers, so if you're not able to multi-shot, they might be
worth considering.  Although I rather think that the weight
would argue against it.

> > The advantages of daggers are simple: you don't have to
> > unwield your melee weapon to throw them (effectively), you
> > don't automatically loose some, and the +2 to hit.  The
> > advantages of arrows is a lot less weight, and more damage
> > per projectile.  Depending on the character or the
> > situation, one or the other can predominate---a ranger who
> > stumbles on three or four arrow traps in the first level of
> > the mines is likely to be better off using arrows than
> > daggers, and of course, in the late game, when your luck is
> > maxed out and you've blessed them (so losses are minimal),
> > and you're hitting at 100% anyway, arrows beat daggers
> > consistently, except if you're really meleeing most of the
> > time, and want to keep that melee weapon in hand.

> Barbarians only get expert at weapon classes without artifacts
> except Cleaver, so I tend to see them as having lots of skill
> slots available as they increase their XP.  Three to get
> skilled in attack spells?  Could well happen once dragon scale
> mail comes available.  One each for dagger and bow missiles
> can be used to okay effect.

Becauase there's nothing a Barbarian can multifire, they're
basically melee fighters.  Which means the fact that you have to
change the wielded weapon argues against bow and arrow.  To
date, I've always used daggers (and in later parts of the game,
attack spells even more than daggers) with them.

